I wouldn't call this the kind of unavoidable death that justifies 
a backup file.  Can't kick things out in 3.1 -- as it should be.  
Even the pet trick is too easy.  Engraving Elbereth is tough without
an athame to engrave with, and without a levitation item you would
have scuffled it if you tried to fight while standing on it.  (Hearsay,
as I don't do Elbereth.  :-> )  Don't resort to backup files; just
find another pet who'll steal for you (throw any cat or dog food), or 
a really big pet who'll kill the shopkeeper for you, or lots of gold, 
or a wand of polymorph, or a wand of death, or ...

(I tend to use exclusively pets to steal from shops.  Other methods
tend to get my next character with the same name killed, even when
they work.)

> BTW-- How does the djinni(sp)/lamp thing work?

There are magic lamps and oil lamps, which are indistinguishable 
without either Identify, or leaving the sucker on forever and seeing
if it goes out (or rubbing for a djinn, which is a bad idea as I
mentioned above).  I don't know the percentages off the top of my 
head, but your odds of getting a happy djinn who'll give you a wish 
are significantly better if you make sure the magic lamp is blessed 
before you rub it.  Brass lanterns are easily distinguished, and the 
game makes fun of you if you try to rub them.

I often keep a magic lamp around as a light source, even after I've
blessed it.  I just hate darkness...  Causes me to run into things
like an idiot and lose perfectly good games.

